{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","text":"The four rules","type":"heading","level":2},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Magnification \/ Pinch","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MagnifyGesture"},{"type":"text","text":" (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.PopSwitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Pop Switch","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" flipped on a threshold, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".spring"},{"type":"text","text":" pop (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body. Origami ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers